The retained replay supports the seven classifications claimed, and the code explains the `-c` refusal. It does not establish semantic adequacy. The main draft weakness is that its third acceptance item calls an architectural exclusion a “red control”; that exclusion can constrain the recommendation, but it does not test whether a proposed warning catches useful mistakes.

